Live Translate 01
=================

APLUX-authored application code and interfaces retain their designated Apache-2.0
terms. The reused native transcription and translation SDKs retain their scoped
Pandora terms and applicable third-party rights.

The transcription and translation SDKs are referenced as fixed Git submodules from:
  https://github.com/APLUX-Pandora/audio8-asr-infinite-demo
  https://github.com/APLUX-Pandora/hy-mt2-1.8b-demo
Preserve the license and notice files accompanying each SDK when redistributing
those components. The application stores component Git links rather than copied native libraries,
headers or bindings. Recursive clone retrieves the original component trees; model
packages are obtained separately.

The separately downloaded transcription package includes Silero VAD under its
MIT terms; LICENSES/Silero-VAD-MIT.txt is preserved here as well. Other model
assets remain in their original repositories with their accompanying terms.
AidLite, AidGen, Qualcomm QNN/QAIRT and operating-system runtimes are external
platform components and are not distributed in this application tree.

Input lecture files are not bundled. APLUX/Pandora marks are brand assets.
No speaker, media producer or third-party project endorsement is implied.

